<title>FRANCE: Eurotunnel to convert 8 bln Ffr of debt.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel to convert 8 bln Ffr of debt.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French channel tunnel operator Eurotunnel said on Monday that eight billion francs of its junior debt would be converted into shares at 10.40 francs per share.</p>
<p>The company also said it would issue eight billion francs of December 2003 convertible bonds that would be converted at a price of 12.40 francs per share.</p>
<p>The announcement was part of a debt restructuring deal aimed at insuring the long term viability of Eurotunnel. Under the agreement, shareholders will hold 54.5 percent of the company's capital after the restructuring.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
